{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5no58DSFg1JPPCR7vwM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I've analyzed the repository. Here's my summary:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt:11-16` — no status field currently\n- Shipment entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-14` — already has ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- OrderController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt:17-46` — has POST /orders, GET /orders/{orderId}, GET /orders\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:22-56` — has POST /shipments, GET /shipments/{shipmentId}, GET /shipments\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` — defines error codes\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Error handling uses sealed ApiException hierarchy (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler centralizes error response formatting\n- Tests use MockMvc with assertions on both status and error code/message\n- In-memory repositories for test startup speed\n- Controllers inject repositories and throw exceptions for failures\n\n**Affected files (must change):**\n1. `Order.kt` — add status field (OrderStatus enum)\n2. `OrderController.kt` — add POST cancel endpoint\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` — add method to find shipments by orderId\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — add method to find shipments by orderId\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — check order status before allowing shipment creation\n6. `ApiError.kt` — add ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — add tests for cancel functionality\n8. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add test for rejecting shipment on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n- Idempotent retry behavior must work — cancelling an already-cancelled order succeeds silently\n- All-or-nothing atomicity — if any shipment is CONFIRMED, entire cancel fails and state remains unchanged\n- Race conditions in concurrent environment — need atomic check-and-update logic\n- Existing tests must not break\n\n**Open questions:** None — the ticket is clear on all scenarios.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field and `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) to track order lifecycle.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add POST `/orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that:\n   - Throws 404 (ResourceNotFoundException) if order doesn't exist\n   - Succeeds (200 OK) if order already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Checks all shipments for CONFIRMED status; if found, throws 409 ConflictException without changing state\n   - Updates order to CANCELLED and updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Returns the cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Inject OrderRepository and check order status in create endpoint; throw 409 if order is CANCELLED.\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code for the shipment-on-cancelled-order rejection.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests:\n   - Cancel an active order → 200 OK, order becomes CANCELLED\n   - Repeated cancel of same order → 200 OK, no change (idempotency)\n   - Cancel when a shipment is CONFIRMED → 409 Conflict, order stays ACTIVE\n   - Cancel non-existent order → 404 Not Found\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test:\n   - Create shipment for cancelled order → 409 Conflict with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a database transaction for atomicity: Rejected because the system already uses in-memory storage with ConcurrentHashMap. Transactions would require adding persistence, which violates \"no new dependencies.\"\n- Soft-deleting orders: Rejected because the ticket explicitly requires status tracking as ACTIVE/CANCELLED, not deletion.\n- Checking order existence in ShipmentController by making it optional: Rejected because the ticket states \"Creating a shipment for an order that does not exist keeps its current behaviour\" — meaning we only reject for CANCELLED orders, not non-existent ones.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Scenario | Read | Check | Write | Response |\n|----------|------|-------|-------|----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | order, shipments | none CONFIRMED | order→CANCELLED, matching shipments→CANCELLED | 200 + order |\n| Cancel already CANCELLED order | order | (none needed, idempotent) | (nothing) | 200 + order |\n| Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment | order, shipments | any CONFIRMED | (nothing) | 409 CONFLICT |\n| Cancel non-existent order | (nothing) | order exists | (nothing) | 404 NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | order | order.status==CANCELLED | (nothing) | 409 CONFLICT (ORDER_CANCELLED) |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest.cancelOrder_cancelsActiveOrder** — creates order, cancels it, verifies status changes to CANCELLED and shipments are cancelled\n2. **OrderControllerTest.cancelOrder_idempotent** — cancels same order twice, second succeeds with no change\n3. **OrderControllerTest.cancelOrder_blockedByConfirmedShipment** — creates shipment, confirms it, cancel fails with 409, order still ACTIVE\n4. **OrderControllerTest.cancelOrder_notFound** — cancel non-existent order returns 404\n5. **ShipmentControllerTest.createShipment_rejectedForCancelledOrder** — create order, cancel it, create shipment fails with 409\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me now implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":974,"cache_read_input_tokens":21853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemera