t | Added ShipmentRepository injection and POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint | Required — ticket asks for new cancel endpoint |\n| ShipmentRepository.kt | Added findByOrderId() method | Required — needed to find shipments for an order to cancel |\n| ShipmentController.kt | Added OrderRepository injection and check for CANCELLED orders | Required — ticket asks to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders |\n| ApiError.kt | Added ORDER_CANCELLED error code | Required — needed for shipment-on-cancelled-order rejection |\n| OrderControllerTest.kt | Added 5 new tests for cancel functionality | Required — ticket acceptance criteria 5 demands test coverage |\n| ShipmentControllerTest.kt | Added 1 new test for cancelled order rejection | Required — ticket acceptance criteria 5 demands test coverage |\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None\n\nAll acceptance criteria are satisfied, no forbidden files were modified, and the implementation preserves the existing architecture.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Customers can cancel orders that haven't had shipments confirmed by a carrier, with status tracking (ACTIVE/CANCELLED), all-or-nothing semantics, and idempotent retry behavior.\n\nChanged       Order.kt — added status field and OrderStatus enum\n              OrderController.kt — added cancel endpoint with all-or-nothing logic\n              ShipmentRepository.kt — added findByOrderId method\n              ShipmentController.kt — added validation to reject shipments for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt — added ORDER_CANCELLED error code\n              OrderControllerTest.kt — added 5 tests for cancel scenarios\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 1 test for cancelled order rejection\n\nTests         OrderControllerTest: cancels an active order and returns 200 (status changes to CANCELLED)\n              OrderControllerTest: repeated cancel of same order succeeds idempotently (retry safety)\n              OrderControllerTest: cancels all CREATED shipments when cancelling order (shipment update)\n              OrderControllerTest: cancel fails with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (all-or-nothing)\n              OrderControllerTest: cancel returns 404 for non-existent order (404 handling)\n              ShipmentControllerTest: rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order (409 ORDER_CANCELLED)\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 19, Failures: 0, Errors: 0\n\nNot done      None — all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no forbidden files modified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3299,"cache_read_input_tokens":35132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3299},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9721380-5fc1-442d-b270-a30cdb5c7cd2","uuid":"650f41f7-34f2-46fa-bb73-89c9191a07d9","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:40:20.758Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5nvu8ATuzh169bZQUDH"}
